  "description": "Test your problem-solving, DSA, Java programming, and DBMS skills through a company-style Online Assessment. The challenge includes coding problems and technical MCQs designed to evaluate logical thinking, technical fundamentals, and algorithmic efficiency . Guidelines: The assessment consists of 2 coding questions, 2 DBMS MCQs, and 5 Java MCQs . The coding questions will focus on DSA, algorithms, and problem-solving . Candidates must carefully read the problem statement, input/output format, and constraints before attempting each coding question. Coding solutions should be optimized to handle the given constraints and edge cases. MCQs will test conceptual understanding as well as practical programming knowledge. Candidates should manage their time effectively across coding and MCQ sections. Hidden test cases may be used to evaluate coding submissions. Rules: The assessment duration is 60 minutes . Candidates must submit their own work. Plagiarism, copying, or use of unauthorized external assistance is strictly prohibited. Candidates must use only the programming language(s) permitted for the assessment. Once the assessment time expires, submissions will be automatically closed. Candidates should ensure a stable internet connection throughout the assessment. Any attempt to manipulate the assessment platform or bypass its evaluation system may result in disqualification . The final score will be based on the correctness of coding submissions and MCQ responses.",
